\f0\b\fs48 \cf0 Total Global Clarification
\f1\b0\fs24 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sl360\slmult1\qc\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 55 years Before The Dawkinis
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sl360\slmult1\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf0 Pathetic rays of sunlight barely penetrated the permanent layer of condensation, emissions and miscellaneous airborne particulate matter known as \'93the layer.\'94 Decade upon decade of fossil fuel emissions, chemical misuse, pesticides and cow farts had pushed the atmosphere well beyond the point of no return. No meaningful attempt was made to reverse the degradation of the environment. There was no profit in that. The natural and according to the company, rational course of action was to spew yet more noxious chemicals into the atmosphere. Unprecedented amounts of \'93air-cleaner\'94 over extended periods. The sales pitch to the world was \'93total atmospheric clarification\'94. Clean air, clean living and, with \'93Marlborough Country\'94 ads once again possible, a surge in cigarette sales.
\f1 \

\f2 Governments everywhere swallowed the hype without question. Why would they questions it\cf2 ? \cf0 Some of the greatest scientific minds on the planet (that are employed by the company) concluded that this was the only solution to global air pollution. Sales went beyond anyone\'92s wildest expectations. Financially, the company and the Primary Trade Dominion really cleaned up, unfortunately however, the atmosphere did not. Rather than clarifying\'94 the air, all pollutants condensed together at about 300 metres above sea level. A floating pea-soup acid-mist representing the sum of all the filth and foul muck ever spewed out of a smoke stack, exhaust pipe, chimney or cow\'92s bum. Pure concentrated evil. 
\f1 \

\f2 Governments from all over the world protested, sent envoys and some even threatened military action. The company \'93CEO\'94 laughed at that prospect, Western \cf2 Ulyssia\cf0  was a nuclear wasteland and PTD now manufactured most of the world\'92s armaments and all of the high-tech bio-weapons. Very few had the balls to attack and even fewer had sufficient armaments to sustain such unwise undertaking. The company explained to their disgruntled customers that the process had not failed, it had merely worked in an unexpected way. The final desired result would merely take a little longer and require the purchase of more product. With the addition of a little dye in the mixture, \'93the layer\'94 was changed from spew green to a pleasant silvery white hue. Apart from the aesthetic improvement, the extra purchases did nothing to alleviate the problem. 
\f1 \

\f2 The layer blocked half of the sunlight and, as such, was insufficient to allow photosynthesis to take place. Poor and low-lying countries were first to die out. No sun, no crops and no life. Unless they possessed enclosed habitats and radiation shielding, communities at higher altitudes fared little better. In the space of 20 years the world\'92s population shrank by 62%. Places fit for human habitation were reduced by 80%. The sins of old Ulyssia were visited upon the entire world.
\f1 \

